      "message": "Hmm ... I\u0027m not sure I understand the above comment. The approach of this patch is to allow bvec_split_segs() to build bvecs larger than the segment size (4 KiB) and to split these later. Splitting later either happens by blk_rq_map_sg() (used by e.g. the SCSI core) or by the following changes applied to the null_blk driver:\n\n```\n        rq_for_each_segment(bvec, rq, iter) {\n-               len \u003d bvec.bv_len;\n+               len \u003d min(bvec.bv_len, nullb-\u003edev-\u003emax_segment_size);\n+               bvec.bv_len \u003d len;\n```",
